Tool.
  tool """" KeYmaera X """"
  model """" ArchiveEntry "Theorem C2: oscillation threshold beta*Ks > b^2/4"

/* The (delta,dw) subsystem  delta'=dw, dw'=-b*dw-beta*Ks*delta  has companion
 * matrix [[0,1],[-beta*Ks,-b]] with characteristic polynomial
 *      lambda^2 + b*lambda + beta*Ks.
 * Its discriminant is b^2 - 4*beta*Ks.  The eigenvalues are a complex
 * (oscillatory) pair iff the discriminant is negative, i.e.
 *      beta*Ks > b^2/4 ,
 * in which case the real part is -b/2 and the natural frequency is
 *      omega_osc = sqrt(beta*Ks - b^2/4).
 * In particular Ks = 0 (bare GFL, Power Lock) gives discriminant b^2 >= 0:
 * eigenvalues {0,-b}, both real -- the frequency mode never oscillates.
 *
 * Pure first-order real-arithmetic equivalence, parametric in b, beta, Ks.
 * MACHINE-CHECKED: KeYmaera X 5.1.2 reports `proved` (QE, Z3 backend). See
 * ../results/keymaerax_proof_log.txt.
 */

Problem
  \forall b \forall beta \forall Ks
  ( b > 0 & beta > 0 & Ks > 0
    -> ( (b^2 - 4*beta*Ks < 0) <-> (beta*Ks > b^2/4) ) )
End.

Tactic "oscillation threshold by real arithmetic"
  QE
End.

End. """"
  tactic """" QE """"
  proof """"  """"
End.
